.nh
.TH "PB-DOMAIN-ADD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-domain-add - Add a domain and show its DNS records


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb domain add <domain> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a domain you control to the active workspace and print the DNS records to create at your
DNS provider: a CNAME that proves you control it, and the records that point names at
Paperboat. Then run pb domain verify. Once the domain is verified, any name one level under it
works with --domain on tunnels and previews.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb domain add dev.example.com
  pb domain add dev.example.com --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-domain(1)\fP
